9b74893594-parent\",{\"data-identity\":\"unordered-list\",\"className\":\"my-rem16px mx-0 pl-[1.25rem] list-disc marker:text-brandBlue-500 print:marker:text-black marker:pl-rem24px print:my-rem8px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal  \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"769b74893594\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"5bd8ae1f34c8\",{\"children\":[\"First-degree burn\"]}],\": A superficial and generally mild skin injury. Examples would include sunburn or the tenderness you feel after briefly touching a plate that’s too hot (even though the waitress warned you).\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"6ba118e9bdee\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"e90f226d53f5\",{\"children\":[\"Second-degree burn\"]}],\": These burns affect both the top (epidermis) and second (dermis) layers of skin. Blistering is possible. Scarring may occur. This type of burn could be caused by a hot water spill or touching a hot stove.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"f0b934b99032\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"0eb43ea19692\",{\"children\":[\"Third-degree burn\"]}],\": These burns extend past the skin into deeper body tissue, like fat, muscle or even bone. Damage can be severe. It could be caused by prolonged contact with fire or hot metal, or electrical or chemical burns.\"]}]]}]\n3e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"d4b9a8c51a5f\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Any burn believed to be worse than a first-degree burn \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"c9efb6281779\",{\"children\":[\"should be seen by a medical professional immediately\"]}],\", advises Dr. Capin. Quick treatment reduces the risk of an infection that could complicate recovery.\"]}]\n3f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"70620f421079\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"“The more time you take, the higher the likelihood you can have an infection or mismanage the treatment of it,” he says. “If you’re not sure what to do, don’t guess: Go to your local urgent care or emergency room immediately.”\"]}]\n40:[\"$\",\"div\",\"70620f421079_mobile_ad\",{\"data-identity\":\"billboard-ad\",\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden pri"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"nt:hidden max-w-[400px] min-w-[300px] m-auto  pt-rem16px pb-[3.125rem] my-rem32px  \",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-[300px] mx-auto\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"horizontal-bar\",\"className\":\"h-[5px] w-[40px] bg-gray-800 \"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 text-rem16px leading-rem23px mt-rem8px mb-rem12px font-bold\",\"children\":\"Advertisement\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden flex-col items-center justify-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"ad-slot\",\"id\":\"billboard2_300x250_mobile\",\"className\":\"ad-reset w-[300px] !min-h-[250px] flex bg-gray-300\"}],null]}]]}]}]\n41:[\"$\",\"h3\",\"3644154e2f3b\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"The 4Cs of burn care\"]}]\n42:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"810fb261b9a2\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"56c68389afcd\",{\"data-identity\":\"figure-container\",\"className\":\"block w-full my-rem32px \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"figure\",null,{\"className\":\"print:hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"className\":\"border-4 border-gray-300 w-full h-auto\",\"src\":\"https://assets.clevelandclinic.org/transform/b44a1c55-09ed-45a1-9b0e-e5f33a27e486/FirstAid-Burns-infographic?io=transform:fit,width:1200\",\"alt\":\"First aid treatment for burns, the 4cs of burn care\",\"loading\":\"lazy\",\"width\":1200,\"height\":1925}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"hidden print:block text-gray-900 text-rem14px leading-rem20px mb-rem8px\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-rem8px\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"Image\",\" content:\"]}],\" This \",\"image\",\" is available to \",\"view\",\" online.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"View image\",\" online\"]}],\" \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-600 text-rem12px break-all\",\"children\":[\"(\",\"https://assets.clevelandclinic.org/transform/b44a1c55-09ed-45a1-9b0e-e5f33a27e486/FirstAid-Burns-infographic\",\")\"]}]]}],\"$undefined\"]}]]}]]}]\n43:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9046e85aaee8\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"The 4Cs of burn care — cooling, cleaning, covering, and comforting — offer a game plan for the all-important initial treatment of burns. Each step plays a role in reducing damage, limiting complications and healing.\"]}]\n44:[\"$\",\"p\",\"c9139204a16d\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Here’s what to do:\"]}]\n45:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"32f2f3792a25-parent\",{\"data-identity\":\"ordered-list\",\"className\":\"my-rem16px mx-0 pl-rem24px list-decimal marker:pl-rem24px print:my-rem8px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal marker:text-brandBlue-500 marker:font-semibold print:marker:text-black  \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"32f2f3792a25\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 mb-rem12px text-rem19px leading-rem34px pl-rem12px print:mb-rem4px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"1007316c8d83\",{\"children\":[\"Cooling\"]}],\": Apply cool water to a burn for five to 20 minutes by gently running tap water over the burn, dipping the burned area in water or using a wet towel. This helps stop the burning process to reduce tissue damage and pain.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"2096875bc025\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 mb-rem12px text-rem19px leading-rem34px pl-rem12px print:mb-rem4px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"7ab172871eba\",{\"children\":[\"Cleaning\"]}],\": Gently cleanse the wound with mild soap and water or an antiseptic solution to remove debris, dirt and bacteria. This lowers the risk of infection, including serious ones like \",["])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\"$\",\"a\",\"11554f7f56e8\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/12361-sepsis\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"sepsis\"]}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"c0fb3944d3f7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 mb-rem12px text-rem19px leading-rem34px pl-rem12px print:mb-rem4px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"14369ee2a726\",{\"children\":[\"Covering\"]}],\": Protect the wound from contamination by covering it with a non-stick sterile dressing. (Plastic wrap can work in a pinch.) This can reduce pain by shielding nerve endings from air exposure and promote healing by maintaining a moist environment.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"35e59df63b80\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 mb-rem12px text-rem19px leading-rem34px pl-rem12px print:mb-rem4px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"c5e81f8a4480\",{\"children\":[\"Comforting\"]}],\": Burn injuries can be painful and distressing. Consider taking an over-the-counter pain medication like ibuprofen (Advil®) or acetaminophen (Tylenol®) for the physical hurt. Staying calm also helps your body heal.\"]}]]}]\n46:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9b174c36007e\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"For more serious burns, a fifth C — “calling” for help — should be included.\"]}]\n47:[\"$\",\"div\",\"9b174c36007e_mobile_ad\",{\"data-identity\":\"billboard-ad\",\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden print:hidden max-w-[400px] min-w-[300px] m-auto  pt-rem16px pb-[3.125rem] my-rem32px  \",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-[300px] mx-auto\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"horizontal-bar\",\"className\":\"h-[5px] w-[40px] bg-gray-800 \"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 text-rem16px leading-rem23px mt-rem8px mb-rem12px font-bold\",\"children\":\"Advertisement\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden flex-col items-center justify-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"ad-slot\",\"id\":\"billboard6_300x250_mobile\",\"className\":\"ad-reset w-[300px] !min-h-[250px] flex bg-gray-300\"}],null]}]]}]}]\n48:[\"$\",\"h3\",\"1ec3fa406173\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"The don’ts of treating a burn\"]}]\n49:[\"$\",\"ul\",\"0b2f5d22ea34-parent\",{\"data-identity\":\"unordered-list\",\"className\":\"my-rem16px mx-0 pl-[1.25rem] list-disc marker:text-brandBlue-500 print:marker:text-black marker:pl-rem24px print:my-rem8px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal  \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"0b2f5d22ea34\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"c1d025d3ca84\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",\"c1d025d3ca84\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://health.clevelandclinic.org/should-you-put-ice-on-a-burn-or-not\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"Never use ice\"]}],\" or ice-cold water\"]}],\", as this could reduce blood flow to the injured area and delay healing.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"74e05d0c6ff8\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"8fd8bfdf1bad\",{\"children\":[\"Don’t use water that might be contaminated\"]}],\", like from a lake, river or stream. Bacteria in the water may cause an inf"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ection.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"36282b115768\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"7c405a2b8f27\",{\"children\":[\"Don’t pull stuck clothing away from a burn. \"]}],\"Forcing it off may tear away skin and worsen your wound. Leave the removal to healthcare professionals in a safe environment.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"ff377bb480b1\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"d33a20676a4e\",{\"children\":[\"Never pop a burn blister\"]}],\". The skin beneath the blistered area can easily become infected. If a blister pops on its own naturally, cover the area until you’re able to see a healthcare provider.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"36743a7b1e2e\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"e0c67fe963e7\",{\"children\":[\"Don’t use any ointments or sprays\"]}],\". Butter, oil, ointment and first-aid sprays can slow the release of heat from your skin, making the wound worse.\"]}]]}]\n4a:[\"$\",\"h3\",\"51a980fea84b\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"When to seek medical care\"]}]\n4b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"59acc086c457\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Any burn beyond the skin surface or involving broken skin should be seen by a healthcare provider right away. They’ll be able to assist with cleaning and treating the burn, as well as provide stronger forms of \",[\"$\",